</maxScale></scaleRange><ArcGISProfile>ItemDescription</ArcGISProfile></Esri><dataIdInfo><idPurp>Sample collection locations on Apollo 12 EVA 1.</idPurp><idAbs>&lt;DIV STYLE="text-align:Left;"&gt;&lt;DIV&gt;&lt;DIV&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN&gt;Shapefile containing the mapped locations of the geology samples collected during EVA 1 of Apollo 12.  In some cases, a sample ID could not be assigned to a single location, either because samples collected over a broad area were combined into a single bag or because of insufficient information about the sample at time of collection.  In these cases, sample IDs were recorded in all locations where they may have been collected.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN /&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN&gt;Note: EVA 1 samples 12002, 12003, 12005, 12009, 12011, 12012, and 12018 were unable to be located and do not appear in this dataset.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN /&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN&gt;Locations were mapped relative to the NAC_DTM_APOLLO12 orthophoto NAC_DTM_APOLLO12_M120005333_50CM.TIF, in an Equirectangular Moon projected coordinate system centered on 3°S, 180°E.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN&gt;To see mapped data in context of the mission transcript, see APOLLO_12-1_DETAILED_TRANSCRIPT.CSV&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN /&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN&gt;Attribute field descriptions:&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN&gt;Bag: Bag in which the astronaut collected the sample(s).&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN&gt;ID: Sample ID number(s), in range format.  If samples were numbered out of order, sample ID numbers may fall within an ID range of a location where they were not collected.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN&gt;IDList: Sample ID number(s), in list format.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN&gt;IDListCont: Overflow column for listed sample IDs.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN&gt;G_E_Time: Timestamp associated with sample(s), in ground-elapsed time (time since liftoff, reported in hours:minutes:seconds).&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN&gt;Type: Sample type (core, rake, soil, etc).&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN&gt;Station: Station at which the astronaut collected the sample(s).&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;</idAbs><idCredit>Gonzales et al. (2020) LPS LI, Abstract #1578.  https://www.hou.usra.edu/meetings/lpsc2020/pdf/1578.pdf</idCredit><idCitation><resTitle>Apollo 12 EVA 1 Samples</resTitle></idCitation><searchKeys><keyword>Moon</keyword><keyword>lunar</keyword><keyword>Apollo</keyword><keyword>Apollo 12</keyword></searchKeys></dataIdInfo><mdHrLv><ScopeCd value="005"/></mdHrLv><mdDateSt Sync="TRUE">20250828</mdDateSt></metadata>
